# TDD Enforcement

## Refactor discipline

- Before refactoring, ensure a failing test exists that captures current behavior or the bug.
- If no test exists, write one first; run it; confirm it fails (or passes for the buggy case).
- Refactor; run tests; verify they pass.
- Do not refactor without test coverage for the affected code path.

## Exceptions

- Pure formatting/style changes (no behavior change) may skip new tests.
- Documentation-only changes do not require tests.
- When adding tests is infeasible (e.g. third-party integration), document the risk and get explicit approval.

## Verification

- Run `npm test` before committing any refactor.
- Run `npm run compile` to catch type errors.
- If tests fail after a refactor, revert or fix before pushing.
